</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Semantic Correctness</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Results are shown in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2 Semantic Correctness ‣ 4 Results ‣ Formalizing Numerical Analysis: An Agent Pipeline and Quality Audit Beyond Kernel Acceptance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Agreement percentage is found by comparing results from NL vs. Lean and NL vs. back-
translated NL after grouping faithful and stronger categories together.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S4.T2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Semantic correctness evaluation across formalization systems via NL vs. Lean (direct, DeepSeek) and NL vs. back-translated NL (round-trip, GPT-oss-120b). Faithful = formalization is logically equivalent to source; Stronger = formalization entails source; Different = formalization diverges from source. <sup id="S4.T2.5.1" class="ltx_sup">†</sup>Agreement is computed by grouping faithful and stronger together.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S4.T2.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T2.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"></th>
<th id="S4.T2.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"></th>
<td id="S4.T2.6.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">OpenMath</span></td>
<td id="S4.T2.6.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.6.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">M2F</span></td>
